          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The notion of
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-congruence"} 2-congruence
            is the generalization of the notion of
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/congruence"} congruence
            from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theory
            to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category+theory"} 2-category theory
          %p
            The correct notions of
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+2-category"} regularity
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+2-category"} exactness
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-categories"} 2-categories
            is one of the subtler parts of the theory of first-order structure. In particular, we need a suitable replacement for the 1-categorical notion of
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+relation"} equivalence relation
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/StreetCBS"} StreetCBS
          %p
            One way to express the idea is that in an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-category"} n-category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+logic"} internally
            a
            = succeed "-category;" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n-1)
            = succeed "-category\u201D" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n-1)
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n=1
            = succeed ";" do
              %em equivalence relation
            = succeed "\u201D" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+category"} internal 1-category
          %p
            Of course, there is an obvious notion of an internal category in a 2-category, as a straightforward generalization of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+category"} internal categories
            in a 1-category. But internal categories in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
            are
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+categories"} double categories
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+categories"} double categories
            to those that really represent honest
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1-categories"} 1-categories
            = succeed "." do
              %em 2-congruences
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            Before we define 2-congruences below in def.
            = succeed "," do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#2Congruence"}
          %h3#2congruences 2-Congruences
          #HomWiseDiscreteInternalCategory.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              is a finitely complete 2-category, a
              %strong homwise-discrete category
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              consists of
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+morphism"} discrete morphism
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi D
                            %mn 1
                          %mo →
                          %msub
                            %mi D
                            %mn 0
                          %mo ×
                          %msub
                            %mi D
                            %mn 0
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D_1\to D_0\times D_0
              %li
                %p
                  with composition and identity maps
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi D
                          %mn 0
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi D
                          %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D_0\to D_1
                  and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi D
                          %mn 1
                        %msub
                          %mo ×
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi D
                              %mn 0
                        %msub
                          %mi D
                          %mn 1
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi D
                          %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D_1\times_{D_0} D_1\to D_1
                  in
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi K
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi D
                            %mn 0
                          %mo ×
                          %msub
                            %mi D
                            %mn 0
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K/(D_0\times D_0)
            %p
              which satisfy the usual axioms of an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+category"} internal category
              up to
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            %p
              Together with the evident notions of
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+functor"} internal functor
              and
              %strong
                internal
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
              there is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi HDC
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} HDC(K)
              of hom-wise discrete 2-categories in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              Since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi D
                      %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi D
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ×
                    %msub
                      %mi D
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D_1\to D_0\times D_0
              is discrete, the structural isomorphisms will automatically satisfy any
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherence"} coherence
              axioms one might care to impose.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              The transformations between functors
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                    %mo →
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D\to E
              are a version of the notion for internal categories, thus given by a morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi D
                      %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D_0\to E_1
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi D
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(D_0,E_0)
              play no explicit role, but we will recapture them below.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_3 Remark
            %p
              By homwise-discreteness, any “
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modification"}> modification
              ” between transformations is necessarily a unique isomorphism, so (after performing some quotienting, if we want to be pedantic) we really have a 2-category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi HDC
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} HDC(K)
              rather than a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/3-category"} 3-category
          #Kernel.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:A\to B
              is any morphism in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi A
                      %mo ×
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f/f) \to A\times A
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f/f)
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comma+object"} comma object
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              with itself. We call this the
              %strong kernel
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ker
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ker(f)
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              (the “comma
              = succeed "\u201D" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kernel+pair"} kernel pair
              = succeed "\u201D" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cech+nerve"} Cech nerve
              = succeed ")." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            %p
              In particular, if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mn 1
                      %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f=1_A
              then
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mn 1
                        %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %msub
                        %mn 1
                        %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %msup
                        %mi A
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (1_A/1_A) = A^{\mathbf{2}}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mn 2
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                    %mo ×
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A^{\mathbf{2}} \to A\times A
              called the
              %strong kernel
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ker
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ker(A)
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_4 Remark
            %p
              It is easy to check that taking kernels of objects defines a functor
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Φ
                      %mo :
                      %mi K
                      %mo →
                      %mi HDC
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi K
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi:K \to HDC(K)
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "http://www.springerlink.com/content/407n62422140864p/"} Street
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#InclusionOfKernelsInCongruences"}
              below.
          #Folding.num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi D
                      %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ⇉
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi D
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D_1\,\rightrightarrows\, D_0
              is a homwise-discrete category in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi D
                          %mn 0
                        %mo ←
                        %msub
                          %mi D
                          %mn 1
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi D
                          %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D_0 \leftarrow D_1 \to D_0
                  is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/two-sided+fibration"} two-sided fibration
                  in
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi K
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              %li
                %p
                  There is a functor
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ker
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi D
                          %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo →
                        %mi D
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ker(D_0)\to D
                  whose object-map
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi D
                          %mn 0
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi D
                          %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D_0\to D_0
                  is the identity.
          %p
            Actually, homwise-discreteness is not necessary for this result, but we include it to avoid worrying about
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherence"} coherence
            isomorphisms, and since that is the case we are most interested in here.
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              We consider the case
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                      %mo =
                      %mi Cat
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K=Cat
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat
              is, essentially, a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+category"} double category
              whose horizontal 2-category is homwise-discrete (hence equivalent to a
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1-category"} 1-category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi D
                      %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi D
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ×
                    %msub
                      %mi D
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D_1\to D_0\times D_0
              by an
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isofibration"} isofibration
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/companion+pair"} companion
              for any vertical arrow.
            %p
              Suppose first that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi D
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ←
                    %msub
                      %mi D
                      %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi D
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D_0 \leftarrow D_1 \to D_0
              is a two-sided fibration. Then for any (vertical) arrow
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi x
                    %mo →
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:x\to y
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi D
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D_0
              we have
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+morphism"} cartesian
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opcartesian+morphisms"} opcartesian morphisms
              (squares) in
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi D
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D_1
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi x
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi id
                          %mtd
                            %mi x
                          %mtd
                            %mspace{:width => "2em"}
                          %mtd
                            %mi x
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi f
                                  %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mi y
                            %mo ′
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mo ≅
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %mi opcart
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi f
                          %mtd
                            %mspace{:width => "2em"}
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mi f
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %mi cart
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mo ≅
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi x
                            %mo ′
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi f
                                  %mn 2
                          %mtd
                            %mi y
                          %mtd
                            %mspace{:width => "2em"}
                          %mtd
                            %mi y
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi id
                          %mtd
                            %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    x &amp; \overset{id}{\to} &amp; x
                    \&amp; \qquad  &amp;
                    x &amp; \overset{f_1}{\to} &amp; y'
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{\cong}}\downarrow &amp; opcart &amp;  \downarrow^{\mathrlap{f}}
                    \&amp; \qquad  &amp;
                    {}^{\mathllap{f}}\downarrow &amp; cart &amp;  \downarrow^{\mathrlap{\cong}}
                    \\\
                    x' &amp; \overset{f_2}{\to} &amp; y
                    \&amp; \qquad &amp;
                    y &amp; \overset{id}{\to} &amp; y
                    }
            %p The vertical arrows marked as isomorphisms are so by one of the axioms for a two-sided fibration. Moreover, the final compatibility axiom for a 2-sided fibration says that the square
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi x
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi f
                                  %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mi y
                            %mo ′
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≅
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mo ≅
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi x
                            %mo ′
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi f
                                  %mn 2
                          %mtd
                            %mi y
                            %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{ x &amp; \overset{f_1}{\to} &amp; y'\\
                    \\cong \downarrow &amp; &amp; \downarrow\cong \\
                    x' &amp; \overset{f_2}{\to} &amp; y,}
            %p
              induced by factoring the horizontal identity square of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              through these cartesian and opcartesian squares, must be an isomorphism. We can then show that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_1
              (or equivalently
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_2
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/companion+pair"} companion
              for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              just as in (
              %a{:href => "#Shulman07"}> Shulman 07, theorem 4.1
              ). Conversely, from a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/companion+pair"} companion pair
              we can show that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi D
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ←
                    %msub
                      %mi D
                      %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi D
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D_0 \leftarrow D_1 \to D_0
              is a two-sided fibration just as as in
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "#Shulman07"} loc cit
            %p
              The equivalence between the existence of companions and the existence of a functor from the kernel of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi D
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D_0
              is essentially found in (
              %a{:href => "#Fiore06"}> Fiore 06
              ), although stated only for the “edge-symmetric” case. In their language, a kernel
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ker
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ker(A)
              is the double category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo □
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Box A
              of commutative squares in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ker
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi D
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ker(D_0)\to D
              which is the identity on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi D
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D_0
              is a
              %em thin structure
              on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ker
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi D
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ker(D_0)
              has companions, and this property is preserved by any functor
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ker
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi D
                        %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ker(D_0)\to D
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ker
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi D
                        %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ker(D_0)\to D
          %p
            In particular, we conclude that up to isomorphism, there can be at most one functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ker
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi D
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ker(D_0)\to D
            which is the identity on objects.
          #2Congruence.num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              A
              %strong 2-congruence
              in a finitely complete
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              is a homwise-discrete category, def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HomWiseDiscreteInternalCategory"}
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              satisfying the equivalent conditions of Theorem
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Folding"}
          .num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              The kernel
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ker
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ker(A)
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Kernel"}
              of any object is a 2-congruence.
            %p
              More generally, the kernel
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ker
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ker(f)
              of any morphism is also a 2-congruence.
          %h3#2forks_and_quotients 2-Forks and Quotients
          %p
            The idea of a 2-fork is to characterize the structure that relates a morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            to its kernel
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ker
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ker(f)
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            %em quotient
            of a 2-congruence is the couniversal 2-fork constructed from it.
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_5 Definition
            %p
              A
              %strong 2-fork
              in a 2-category consists of a 2-congruence
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi s
                      %mo ,
                      %mi t
                      %mo :
                      %msub
                        %mi D
                        %mn 1
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ⇉
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %msub
                        %mi D
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s,t:D_1\;\rightrightarrows\; D_0
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo :
                      %msub
                        %mi D
                        %mn 0
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi D
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i:D_0\to D_1
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi c
                      %mo :
                      %msub
                        %mi D
                        %mn 1
                      %msub
                        %mo ×
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi D
                            %mn 0
                      %msub
                        %mi D
                        %mn 1
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi D
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c:D_1\times_{D_0} D_1\to D_1
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo :
                      %msub
                        %mi D
                        %mn 0
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:D_0\to X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo :
                    %mi f
                    %mi s
                    %mo →
                    %mi f
                    %mi t
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi:f s \to f t
              such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mi i
                    %mo =
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi i = f
              and such that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi D
                              %mn 1
                            %msub
                              %mo ×
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi D
                                  %mn 0
                            %msub
                              %mi D
                              %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi D
                              %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi D
                              %mn 1
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ⇓
                              %mi ϕ
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi D
                              %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi D
                              %mn 0
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi D
                              %mn 0
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ⇓
                              %mi ϕ
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo ↘
                              %mi f
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mi f
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi D
                              %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi D
                              %mn 0
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi f
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "2em"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "2em"}
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi D
                              %mn 1
                            %msub
                              %mo ×
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi D
                                  %mn 0
                            %msub
                              %mi D
                              %mn 1
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo ↘
                              %mi c
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi D
                              %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi D
                              %mn 0
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ⇓
                              %mi ϕ
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mi f
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi D
                              %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi f
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                            %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    D_1\times_{D_0} D_1 &amp; \to &amp; D_1 &amp; = &amp; D_1\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow &amp; \Downarrow_\phi &amp; \downarrow\\
                    D_1 &amp; \to &amp; D_0 &amp;&amp; D_0\\
                    || &amp;\Downarrow_\phi &amp;&amp; \searrow^f &amp; \downarrow f\\
                    D_1 &amp; \to &amp; D_0 &amp; \overset{f}{\to} &amp; X
                    } \qquad = \qquad
                    \\array{ D_1\times_{D_0} D_1 \\
                    \&amp; \searrow^c\\
                    \&amp;&amp; D_1 &amp; \to &amp; D_0\\
                    \&amp;&amp; \downarrow &amp; \Downarrow_\phi &amp; \downarrow f\\
                    \&amp;&amp; D_1 &amp; \overset{f}{\to} &amp; X.
                    }
          %p
            The comma square in the definition of the kernel of a morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:A\to B
            gives a canonical 2-fork
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ⇉
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi A
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi f
                  %mi B
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f/f) \;\rightrightarrows\; A \overset{f}{\to} B.
          %p It is easy to see that any other 2-fork
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi D
                    %mn 1
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ⇉
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi D
                    %mn 0
                  %mo =
                  %mi A
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi f
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D_1 \;\rightrightarrows\; D_0 = A \overset{f}{\to} B
          %p
            factors through the kernel by an essentially unique functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                  %mo →
                  %mi ker
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D \to ker(f)
            that is the identity on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi D
                    %mn 1
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ⇉
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi D
                    %mn 0
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi f
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D_1 \;\rightrightarrows\; D_0 \overset{f}{\to} X
            is a 2-fork, we say that it equips
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            with an
            %strong action
            by the 2-congruence
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi D
                    %mn 0
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g:D_0\to X
            also has an action by
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
