          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_6 Definition
            %p
              A
              %strong quotient
              for a 2-congruence
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi D
                      %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⇉
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi D
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D_1\;\rightrightarrows\; D_0
              in a 2-category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              is a 2-fork
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi D
                      %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⇉
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi D
                      %mn 0
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi q
                    %mi Q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D_1 \;\rightrightarrows\; D_0 \overset{q}{\to} Q
              such that for any object
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
              defines an equivalence of categories
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Q
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi Act
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi D
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(Q,X) \simeq Act(D,X).
          %p
            A quotient can also, of course, be defined as a suitable
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-categorical+limit"} 2-categorical limit
          .num_lem
            %h6#lemma Lemma
            %p
              The quotient
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
              in any 2-congruence is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/eso+morphism"} eso
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi m
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m\colon A\to B
              is ff, then the square we must show to be a pullback is
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Act
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi D
                            %mo ,
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                          %mtd
                            %mi Act
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi D
                            %mo ,
                            %mi B
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi K
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi D
                              %mn 0
                            %mo ,
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                          %mtd
                            %mi K
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi D
                              %mn 0
                            %mo ,
                            %mi B
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{Act(D,A) &amp; \overset{}{\to} &amp; Act(D,B)\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow\\
                    K(D_0,A)&amp; \underset{}{\to} &amp; K(D_0,B)}
            %p
              But this just says that an action of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              is the same as an action of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              which happens to factor through
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi m
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi m
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m
              is ff.
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_7 Definition
            %p
              A 2-fork
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi D
                      %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⇉
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi D
                      %mn 0
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi f
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D_1 \;\rightrightarrows\; D_0 \overset{f}{\to} X
              is called
              %strong exact
              if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is a quotient of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              %em and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              is a kernel of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
          %p
            This is the 2-categorical analogue of the notion of exact fork in a 1-category, and plays an analogous role in the definition of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+2-category"} regular 2-category
            and an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+2-category"} exact 2-category
          %h3#2CategoryOf2Congruences The 2-category of 2-conguences
          %p
            There is an evident but naive
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
            of 2-congruences in any 2-category. And there is a refined version where internal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functors"} functors
            are replaced by internal
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anafunctors"} anafunctors
          #2CongWithOrdinaryFunctors.num_defn
            %h6#definition_8 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
